  "description": "qou-w6x3 (option 2 of qou-hxz4): re-embedding the binding producer's word on 3A strands does NOT restore level-locality for A >= 3, and the reason is the COUPLING GRAPH, not the generator cycling that #7173 diagnosed. The binding word couples every nucleon pair (C(A,2) inter letters, the complete graph K_A) while a contiguous 3A layout supplies only the path P_A (A-1 adjacencies) -- measured, and exhaustive over all contiguous layouts for A <= 7. Dropping contiguity, K_A is layout-realisable iff A <= 6 (counting bound C(A,2) <= 3A-1, proved for all A; A = 7 exhaustively impossible), but no such layout leaves a single nucleon triple contiguous, so the single-generator intra-nucleon crossings are lost in exchange. Coupling a non-adjacent pair by conjugation instead gives a bond whose generator support is the interval [2, 3A-4]: the segmentation collapses from the mass word's 2A-1 segments of largest size 2 to 3 segments whose largest holds 3A-5 of 3A-1 generators, so the dimension-free property is gone at the first non-adjacent pair. A = 2 is the sole exception -- the deuteron's single pair IS the one adjacency -- and there the character MOVES: same H_6, same 23 letters, only the indexing differs, and chi^lambda differs on the 9 partitions of dimension >= 2 while the two 1-dimensional irreps are blind to the embedding. Option 2 is therefore a re-derivation whose one live case is the deuteron.",
